# case: spawnpoint arguments
step 1: gomcplayer Steve 0 4 0
  count: 1
  feedback: Successfully created the player Steve
step 2: tp Steve 7 4 4
  count: 1
  feedback: Teleported Steve to 7.5, 4.0, 4.5
step 3: spawnpoint
  error: You must specify which player you wish to perform this action on.
step 4: spawnpoint Steve
  count: 1
  feedback: Set Steve's spawn point to (7, 4, 4)
step 5: spawnpoint Steve 1 2 3
  count: 1
  feedback: Set Steve's spawn point to (1, 2, 3)
step 6: spawnpoint Steve 1 2
  error: Usage: /spawnpoint [player] [<x> <y> <z>]
step 7: spawnpoint 1 2 3
  error: Usage: /spawnpoint [player] [<x> <y> <z>]
step 8: spawnpoint Steve 1 2 3 4
  count: 1
  feedback: Set Steve's spawn point to (1, 2, 3)
step 9: setworldspawn
  error: You must specify which player you wish to perform this action on.
step 10: setworldspawn 1 2 3
  count: 1
  feedback: Set the world spawn point to (1, 2, 3)
step 11: setworldspawn 1 2
  error: Usage: /setworldspawn [<x> <y> <z>]
